    "id": "154-93_02",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "During summer to the beginning of autumn, samples of zooplankton were gathered\nbetween water depths 0 and 200 meters weekly from a  fixed station in the\nEnglish Strait, Chile Bay.   Samples were collected by means of a net equipped \nwith a 220  micron mesh.   Investigators studied the behavior of the \nzooplankton with respect to environmental variables that were simulaneously \nrecorded using a CTD sounding profiler Lux.\n\nEn Espanol:\nSemanalmente en una estacion fija, ubicada en el estrecho Ingles frente a Bahia\nChile, durante el verano y comienzo de otono anualmente se han tomado muestras\nde zooplancton en tres estratos comprendidos entre  0 y 200 metros, mediante\nuna red de 220 micrones de abertura de malla, con el proposito de determinar el\ncomportamiento de las especies zooplanctonicas respecto a las variables\nambientales que se han registrado simultaneamente mediante una sonda\nperfiladora CTD Lux.",
